{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/866053-relics-suggestions-ideas","id":866053,"title":"Relics: Suggestions, Ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T12:28:48-07:00","id":866053,"title":"Relics: Suggestions, Ideas?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well once again, I've been hit by a bout of inspiration to start home brewing some Scion material. Specifically directed towards Relics for helping out Scions in their adventures. Below are the ideas I came up with, <i>but if you have your own</i>, please feel free to post them! Also, if you have any thoughts on the ones I came up with, let me know.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Compensator:</b> Spatha (+4L, 1 Purview) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Info:</b> Upon taking a single look at this oversize long sword, a normal warrior would laugh it off as a joke, meant to draw attention away from the user's other short comings. Only a child of the Gods (or someone of similar level of strength) could even hope to wield this thing with one arm. Depending on the culture it was forged by, The Compensator comes in a variety of different shapes and styles. But regardless of who it was forged by, the sword is always meant to be excessively large and heavy. Not only does this oversize blade inflict significantly more damage than a usual sword, but the wielder is able to channel the War Purview as well!<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Desperado:</b> Peacemaker (+1L, -3 Speed, 1 Ability) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Info:</b> Made popular long ago by Scions of the old west, the Desperado is a relic designed for those who take a more <i>&quot;spray and pray&quot;</i> approach to settling disputes. Although its fire power is only slightly higher than normal Peacemakers, it has a jaw dropping rate of fire and never needs to reload.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> Some Legends tell of particularly violent Scions who carry two such pistols at the same time!<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Razor Strings:</b> Garrote Wire (+2L, +2 Defense, 1 Ability) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Info:</b> Although insanely awesome, the use of this weapon would be impractical to those who can't defy the laws of physics. Often requiring the use of special gloves to handle properly, the Razor Strings are a series of sharp, thin wires that the user can manipulate like a puppeteer. In addition to allowing more damage and protection than a standard garrote, the wires can attack from a distance of Legend x5 yards away!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Ritual Mask:</b> (4 Purviews) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Info:</b> A common feature in many pagan religions throughout history, the Egyptians being one of the most well known. The Ritual Mask is a stylized piece of head gear made to invoke the powers of the Gods during religious ceremonies and spells. It is commonly fashioned in the image of a beast's head and can be made from bone, hide, clay or porcelain. When worn, the Ritual Mask allows the user to channel the Animal and Health Purviews, as well as 2 additional Purviews chosen upon the Relic's creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Demon Fork:</b> Iklwa (+2L, 2 Purviews) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Info:</b> Synonymous with evil, this Relic is usually reserved for those who wish to inspire terror and hatred in their wake. Some of the most despised Scions in history carried one of these around with them. The Demon Fork is a two pronged spear that can be repeatedly thrust into its victims. But its true terror comes with the Fire and Death Purviews that it allows the user to channel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-16-2016, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:29:28-07:00","id":866947,"title":"","content":"<b>The Great Club:</b> Macana (+2B, +1 Defense, +2 Accuracy) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Sometimes it just feels good to go savage and beat your enemies to death with a hunk of wood. Like the mighty Heracles of ancient Greece, the Great Club is a primitive but effective weapon given to Scions to aid them in battle. It's shape and style can vary between cultures. To the Irish, it may take the form of a Sheleighleigh, while the Greeks may carve it from a fallen tree trunk. Modern Scions of America may even find it in the form of a baseball bat!<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ninja-to:</b> Wakizashi (+2L, 1 Purview) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Although there is no historical evidence of its existence, the Ninja-to, also known as the Ninja Sword, became popular enough among modern Scions to have them commissioned as Relics. The sword is about the same size as a wakizashi, but the blade is straight instead of curved. When carrying it, it also allows the wielder to channel the Darkness Purview.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Fire Wine:</b> (1 Purview, 1 Ability) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> A popular Relic among Scions who love a good performance. Fire Wine is a bottle containing an extremely flammable alcohol that, while it is safe to drink, is better suited for use in battle. The wine itself allows the owner to channel the Fire Purview, while the bottle is enchanted to replenish it's contents automatically over the course of the night. When fully stocked, the Fire Wine can supply 10 cups worth of drink before it runs empty.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Familiar:</b> (2 Dot Follower) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Many are the stories of witches and sorcerers who travel about with a magical companion known as the Familiar. Often in the form of simple animals, the Familiar has been magically enhanced to make it a more effective servant to their master. The Familiar has mostly the same traits as a typical animal of its species with the following exceptions. The Familiar possesses a Legend rating equal to half it's master's rounded up and gains a free rank of Epic Intelligence and Epic Stamina at creation. For every rank of Legend it possesses, it gains another rank in an Epic Attribute of the player's choice. The Familiar is capable of speaking any language that it's master understands.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> Those who need help selecting a Familiar may use the same list of animals presented for the Nemeans for inspiration.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Bouncing Disk:</b> Discus (+2 Accuracy, 1 Ability, +2L) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Although considered impractical and unwieldy, the idea of a circular boomerang has become a popular craze among Scions today, much to the bemusement (or scorn) of the Gods. By ricocheting off the environment, the Bouncing Disk can hit targets that would have avoided a normal discus, and it always seems to come back to the wielder's hand to provide them with infinite ammunition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:45:10-07:00","id":872770,"title":"","content":"<b>Crucifix:</b> (1 Purview, 1 Ability) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Before it became the religious symbol of Christianity, the crucifix was a favorite instrument of justice for the Roman empire. Some of the more traditionalist Scions of the Dodekatheon may continue to use it as such. Victims would either be tied or nailed to the crucifix while punishment was carried out. Made from two intersecting posts, the crucifix resembles either a T or an X in shape and is commonly fashioned out of wood, though some versions use metal instead. While in proximity of the crucifix, the Scion can channel the Justice Purview and doubles the Duration of associated Boons.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Grimoire:</b> (1 Purview, 2 Abilities) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Even deities have trouble keeping track of all their supernatural powers from time to time, and the Gods of Magic came up with the idea of the Grimoire. This magical research journal allows the scion to channel the Magic Purview and is associated with the Followers Birthright. Should their servants be destroyed, the Grimoire contains a summoning ritual that can completely replenish them, thus overcoming some of the inherent fragility of Followers.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Sleipnir:</b> (3 Purviews, 1 Ability) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> While not as majestic as the actual steed of Odin, The Sleipnir is a bike that would make any leather clad Aesir jealous. This motorcycle grants access to the War, Death and Psychopomp purviews. In addition, the bike handles with a supernatural level of precision, adding the driver's Legend to their Control ability. As its namesake implies, The Sleipnir is typically reserved only for the most impressive scions of the Aesir, commonly the children of Odin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}